 on risk of major adverse cardiovascular event and prior stroke (Pinteraction >0.05 for all). CONCLUSIONS: Semaglutide reduced incidence of any first stroke during the trials versus placebo in people with type 2 diabetes at high cardiovascular risk, primarily driven by small-vessel occlusion prevention. Semaglutide treatment, versus placebo, lowered the risk of stroke irrespective of prior stroke at baseline. REGISTRATION: URL: https://www. CLINICALTRIALS: gov; Unique identifier: NCT01720446 and NCT02692716.

